  "bug": {
    "bug_id": "Codec-15",
    "project": "Codec",
    "summary": "Bug in HW rule in Soundex",
    "description": "The Soundex algorithm says that if two characters that map to the same code are separated by H or W, the second one is not encoded.\n\nHowever, in the implementation (in Soundex.getMappingCode() line 191), a character that is preceded by two characters that are either H or W, is not encoded, regardless of what the last consonant was.\n\nSource: \nhttp://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soundex#American_Soundex"
  },
